    "title": "Understanding ChatGPT Work",
    "summary": "<p>OpenAI <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-for-your-most-ambitious-work/\">announced ChatGPT Work</a> on July 9th, and have been furiously iterating on it ever since. It is an extraordinarily confusing and very powerful product. Here's what I've figured out about it so far.</p> <h4 id=\"two-products\">ChatGPT Work is actually two products</h4> <p>The more interesting version of ChatGPT Work is the one that runs in the cloud. This can be accessed via <a href=\"https://www.chatgpt.com/\">chatgpt.com</a> or through the ChatGPT mobile apps. Let's call it <strong>Work Cloud</strong>.</p> <p>If you install the ChatGPT desktop app - the app that used to be called Codex - you gain access to a thing called ChatGPT Work that can access files and run programs directly on your computer. Let's c...",
